{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 proof of the inequality asked about by Daniel Friedan on MathOverflow 138395: for probability vectors X, Y on n points, 0 ≤ α ≤ 1, zᵢ = Xᵢ^α Yᵢ^{1−α}, K = Σ zᵢ > 0 and Z = z/K, the Shannon entropies satisfy K² H(Z) ≤ α H(X) + (1 − α) H(Y). Also proved: Theorem M, the same inequality for m distributions with weights summing to 1 (zᵢ = ∏ⱼ Xⱼ(i)^{aⱼ}), and Theorem R2, the Rényi-entropy version on two points for every order 0 < γ ≤ 2 log 2, γ ≠ 1, and every m. The two-distribution proof is a descent on the size of the support with concavity arguments for four or more, three and two atoms; Theorem M follows by an index lemma for the Hessian of (Σ eˣⁱ)² H(softmax x) and a maximum principle on faces of the weight simplex.",
